      "check_id": "CKV_AWS_37",
      "title": "IAM user without permissions boundary",
      "resource": "aws_iam_user.privesc15-PassExistingRoleToNewLambdaThenInvoke-user",
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "explanation": "The IAM user does not have a permissions boundary set. Permissions boundaries restrict the maximum permissions an IAM user can have, reducing the risk of privilege escalation."
    }
  ],
  "patched_code": "resource \"aws_iam_user\" \"privesc15-PassExistingRoleToNewLambdaThenInvoke-user\" {\n  name = \"privesc15-PassExistingRoleToNewLambdaThenInvoke-user\"\n  path = \"/\"\n  permissions_boundary = \"arn:aws:iam::123456789012:policy/PermissionsBoundaryPolicy\"\n}",
  "fix_summary": "Added a permissions boundary to the IAM user to restrict its maximum permissions and mitigate privilege escalation risks."
}
